$PT$ and $PQ$ are tangents to the circle, centre $O$, and $\angle TPQ = 38^{\circ}$.
$C$ is a point on the circle in the alternate segment for chord $TQ$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (O) at (3.807,0);
\coordinate (T) at (3.404,1.172);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.404,-1.172);
\draw (O) circle (1.24);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (T);
\draw[tickmark] (P) -- (Q);
\draw (T) -- (Q);
\node[left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\node[below] at (Q) {$Q$};
\coordinate (C) at (5.047,0);
\draw (T) -- (C) -- (Q);
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\pic[draw, "$38^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=Q--P--T};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=T--C--Q};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $x$.

$PC$ and $PQ$ are tangents to the circle, centre $O$, and $PNB$ is a secant, with $N$ the nearer intersection point.
$PN = 4\text{ cm}$ and $NB = 21\text{ cm}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.26]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}
