Find the value of $x$.

$T$ is the point of contact of tangent $TP$ to the circle, centre $O$, with radius $8\text{ cm}$ and $OP = 17\text{ cm}$ (so $PT = 15\text{ cm}$ by Pythagoras' theorem).
$TA$ is a chord, and $B$ is a point on the circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.32]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,8);
\coordinate (L) at (-2,8);
\coordinate (R) at (15.5,8);
\coordinate (P) at (15,8);
\coordinate (A) at (6.632,-4.474);
\coordinate (B) at (-7.518,-2.736);
\draw (O) circle (8);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (L) -- (R);
\draw (O) -- (T);
\draw (O) -- (P);
\draw (T) -- (A);
\draw (T) -- (B);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\node[right] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[left] at (B) {$B$};
\coordinate (ta) at ($(T)!0.3cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (tp) at ($(T)!0.3cm!(P)$);
\draw (ta) -- ($(ta)+(tp)-(T)$) -- (tp);
\pic[draw, "$62^{\circ}$", angle radius=1.1cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--T--R};
\pic[draw, "$y$", angle radius=1cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--B--T};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the value of $y$.

$PC$ is a tangent and $PNB$ is a secant drawn from the external point $P$ to the circle, centre $O$, with $N$ the nearer intersection point.
$PN = 8\text{ cm}$ and $NB = 10\text{ cm}$.
The tangent-chord angle between $PC$ and chord $CN$ is $33.69^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (13,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.923,4.615);
\coordinate (N) at (5,0);
\coordinate (F) at (-5,0);
\draw (O) circle (5);
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above] at (O) {$O$};
\draw (P) -- (C);
\draw (P) -- (F);
\draw (C) -- (N);
\draw (C) -- (F);
\fill (N) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (N) {$N$};
\node[left] at (F) {$B$};
\pic[draw, "$33.69^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=3.6] {angle=N--C--P};
\pic[draw, "$y$", angle radius=0.5cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle=N--F--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Find the length of $PC$.
(b) Find the value of $y$.

